* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-lock-detector-window (issue #38, Part of #16)
* Comparator-window measurement: a BARE delaywin_hv (the four-inverter chain
* plus XC1, the second of this record's two un-swept cap_cmomi instances)
* driven by an ideal step, so the window that sets the whole detector's
* phase-error threshold is measured DIRECTLY rather than inferred from where
* the block's LOCK output happens to change state.
*
* This is the number `spec/porting-plan.md` row 16's ported target
* ("assert window >= 2.5 ns / >= 2x worst static phase offset") applies to.
* The block's coincidence gate is WIDE = ERR AND delaywin_hv(ERR), so an
* XOR(UP,DN) error pulse only produces a WIDE pulse when it is wider than
* this element's LOW-to-HIGH propagation delay -- twin_r below is therefore
* the quantity the phase-error threshold is built out of, and twin_f is
* reported alongside it because the two are not equal in a chain whose last
* node carries an asymmetrically-driven 27 fF MOM load.
*
* run.sh runs this deck FIRST at every corner point, and then scales the
* block-level phase-error ladder (tb_lock_ladder.sp.tmpl) in units of this
* corner's own measured twin_r. That is what makes a fixed relative ladder
* resolve the assert/de-assert thresholds to a fixed FRACTION OF THE WINDOW
* at every corner -- which is exactly the form row 16's hysteresis criterion
* ("hysteresis >= 25% of window") is stated in.
*
* Substituted by ../testbench/run.sh: @CORNER_MOS@, @CORNER_RES@, @TEMP@,
* @VSUP@, @VMID@ (= VSUP/2, pre-computed because ngspice's .meas val= does
* not evaluate a .param expression inside a .control block), @TSTEP@,
* @DUT@ (the MOM-band DUT file mom_inject.py wrote for this run),
* @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ (resolved filesystem path -- ngspice's `.lib`/`.include`
* parser does not expand shell/OS environment variables, issue #54).

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.include @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cap_cmomi.lib
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include @DUT@

Vsub sub! 0 0
Vdd vdd 0 dc @VSUP@

* Ideal step in, 100 ps edges: 20 ns high, then low, inside a 60 ns window,
* so both the rising and the falling propagation delay are measured in one
* transient with the chain fully settled before each edge.
Vstep wstep 0 pulse(0 @VSUP@ 10n 100p 100p 20n 1000n)
Xw wstep wout vdd 0 delaywin_hv

.options reltol=1e-3 abstol=1e-10 vntol=1e-5 chgtol=1e-13
.tran @TSTEP@ 60n

.control
run
meas tran twin_r trig v(wstep) val=@VMID@ rise=1 targ v(wout) val=@VMID@ rise=1
meas tran twin_f trig v(wstep) val=@VMID@ fall=1 targ v(wout) val=@VMID@ fall=1
print twin_r twin_f
.endc
.end
